Ember danced wildly, scattering sparks that blazed and died, bringing no lasting warmth. Shade moved slowly, spreading calm that became stagnant emptiness. The void remained lifeless.

One cycle, they grew weary of their futile efforts. Sitting back-to-back in exhaustion, Ember's heat met Shade's coolness. Where they touched, something unexpected emerged—a gentle rhythm, like breathing.

